Let's expand the powers for $
\left(\blueD{2^4}\right)^{\greenD{2}}=\purpleD{2^n}$.

$\begin{align}
\left(\blueD{2^4}\right)^{\greenD2}&=\underbrace{\blueD{2^4\cdot 2^4}}_\greenD{\text{2 times}}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{
\underbrace{\blueD{2\cdot 2\cdot 2 \cdot 2}}_\text{4 times}
\cdot \underbrace{\blueD{2\cdot 2\cdot 2 \cdot 2}}_\text{4 times}}
_\greenD{\text{2 times}}
\\\\
&=\purpleD{\underbrace{2\cdot 2\cdot 2\cdot 2\cdot  2\cdot  2\cdot  \cdot 2 \cdot 2}_{n\text{ times}}}
\\\\
\end{align}$
